# .worktreeinclude — gitignored files copied into each new Claude Code worktree.
#
# Uses .gitignore syntax. A file is copied only when it BOTH matches a pattern
# here AND is gitignored AND actually exists — tracked files are never
# duplicated, and missing files are silently skipped (so unused patterns no-op).
# Docs: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/worktrees#copy-gitignored-files-into-worktrees
#
# dilenglish is a Next.js app on Firebase App Hosting. The local secrets that a
# worktree needs to run `npm run dev` are the environment files and any local
# key material — both gitignored here (see .gitignore: `.env*`, `*.pem`). New
# worktrees inherit whichever of these exist locally; the rest do nothing.
#
# NOT copied on purpose: node_modules/ (large — run `npm install` per worktree)
# and Next.js build output (.next/ / out/ — regenerated by `npm run build`).

# Local environment files (Next.js / Genkit read these)
.env
.env.local
.env.*

# Local key material (mirrors the .gitignore `*.pem` entry)
*.pem
